@* The interactive root of every circuit. App.razor renders it with InteractiveServer, so it is prerendered first and then
   rendered again once the circuit is connected.

   BrowserNativeSdkInitializer must be inside the interactive tree: on a server every circuit has its own browser services,
   and the initializer starts this circuit's listeners (page lifecycle, connectivity, notification taps, protocol-handler
   links and the cold-start ?bns-notification-click= tap) after the first interactive render. It does nothing while
   prerendering. It lives here rather than in the shared MainLayout because the shared pages also run in the MAUI and WPF
   samples, which don't reference the browser adapter. MainLayout contains <NativeActivationOutlet />, which connects this
   circuit's activation pipeline to its router. *@
